    <string name="help_cookie_title">How to get the Cookie?</string>
    <string name="help_cookie_1">1. Open the login page below in desktop Chrome</string>
    <string name="help_cookie_2">2. Sign in with GitHub / Google (won\'t be blocked)</string>
    <string name="help_cookie_3">3. After login, press F12 → Application → Cookies</string>
    <string name="help_cookie_4">4. Copy all cookies of the site and paste them above</string>
    <string name="help_cookie_5">Format: name1=value1; name2=value2</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_title">How to get OpenCode Go credentials?</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_1">1. Open opencode.ai/auth in desktop Chrome</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_2">2. Sign in with GitHub / Google (Google won\'t block Chrome)</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_3">3. You\'ll land on the dashboard, URL looks like:</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_4">   https://opencode.ai/workspace/{id}/go</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_5">4. Copy the {id} segment → workspaceId</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_6">5. F12 → Application → Cookies</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_7">6. Find the cookie named auth under opencode.ai</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_8">7. Copy its Value field → auth cookie</string>
    <string name="help_ocgo_note">Note: only the auth cookie is needed, not the whole cookie string</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_title">How to get CommandCode Go credentials?</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_1">1. Open https://commandcode.ai and sign in with GitHub</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_2">▸ Get API Key (required):</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_3">   Avatar (top right) → Settings → API Keys → Create a Key</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_4">▸ Get all cookies (for usage records):</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_5">   F12 → Application → Cookies → commandcode.ai</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_6">   Select all cookies and copy the whole string</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_7">   Paste it below — no need to pick them one by one</string>
    <string name="help_ccgo_note">Tip: balance works without cookies, usage records will just be empty.</string>
    <string name="help_codex_title">How to get Codex auth.json?</string>
    <string name="help_codex_1">1. Run codex-oauth-proxy or</string>
    <string name="help_codex_2">   codex-proxy in a terminal to sign in to ChatGPT</string>
    <string name="help_codex_3">2. The credential file is saved at:</string>

